          "severity": "low",
          "summary": "The newly passed note=\"web\" argument has no effect: apply_credit accepts a `note` parameter but never uses it, so the intended provenance tag is silently dropped.",
          "explanation": "The diff changes the call from apply_credit(order[\"invoice\"], order[\"amount\"]) to apply_credit(order[\"invoice\"], order[\"amount\"], note=\"web\"). The call is signature-compatible (note is optional, default \"\"), so it does not raise; however the callee's documented behaviour contract is `def apply_credit(invoice, amount, note=\"\"): \"\"\"Apply a credit given in whole currency units (not cents).\"\"\" invoice[\"credit\"] = amount; return invoice`, i.e. it only assigns the amount and there is no other reference to `note` (the search for note/credit/memo returned only the definition itself). Passing a keyword argument that the implementation ignores gives the false impression that the credit is annotated as originating from the web channel, but no note is recorded anywhere, so downstream consumers of the invoice cannot distinguish this credit from an untagged one. The argument also gives no benefit over the previous call, making the change functionally a no-op that may mask the missing ledger/memo feature.",
